we have an update now from the family of  officer shea  mccolonies last june mcloney's was shot  in the head after  a protest on the strip he was taken to a  special rehab facility in colorado  but is now back home right here in las  vegas reporter kate houston spoke to his  family about his recovery  today i spoke to shea's stepfather  patrick neville he says shea is back  home and now  able to talk and this is great news  after the shooting happened doctors were  not sure if he'd ever speak again  o'shea has been home for a few weeks  after staying at a medical facility in  denver which specializes  in spinal cord injuries his family says  he's still paralyzed and on a ventilator  now shea is going through a transitional  period to adjust to  in-home care his family says being back  in his hometown is a great morale boost  for him  and they're happy he's so close since  he's been home he's been able to see  friends and enjoy the fresh air after  months of rehab  in his hospital room in his house he can  just  go out his bedroom door and he's in his  backyard  his friends can come over and visit with  him he gets to see people we've taken to  the station so he can see his squad  members  um so i think that's really positive for  shay and just to be able to small things  that a lot of people  don't realize is just be able to go  outside  is really a big deal moving forward the  focus is to get shea  stronger and to see him progress even  further  neville says he'd like for shay to also  be around people who are dealing with  the same mobility restrictions  neville says the support from the las  vegas community and from around the  nation has been  outstanding his family is making sure he  sees  all of the calls texts and letters back  to you
 

